speechtext:
For a return showing the revenues collected by the Canadian National Railways for the fiscal years of 1928, 1929, 1930, for the following services at each of the stations hereunder mentioned:
1.	Passenger service in and out-going;
2.	Freight service in and out-going;
3.	Express services, in and out-bound;
4.	Telegraph services out-bound;
Spedden, Ashmount, Owl's _ Eye, St. Paul, Elk Point, Lyndberg and Heinsburg, all in the province of Alberta.
